# MATRU-NETRA: Fix shared patient records

## What changed
- `src/services/patientDataService.ts`: Supabase read/write mapping for maternal patients and visit records.
- `src/context/CareContext.tsx`: loads shared cloud records after login, listens for Supabase Realtime changes, writes registrations/visits to Supabase, and uploads queued registrations/visits when connectivity returns.
- `src/services/authService.ts`: stores the ASHA PHC in `profiles.assigned_phc`, loads pending accounts from Supabase, and uses protected database functions to approve/reject workers.
- `supabase/shared_patient_records.sql`: database migration for PHC-scoped access and protected worker approval.

## Before changing production
1. Back up your Supabase database.
2. Confirm that the existing `maternal_patients` and `visit_records` tables match `supabase/schema.sql`.
3. Open Supabase Dashboard -> SQL Editor.
4. Run `supabase/shared_patient_records.sql`.
5. Make sure each existing ASHA profile has `assigned_phc` set to the exact same text as the patient's `phc_name`. The migration cannot safely guess this for older ASHA accounts. Example (replace the UUID and PHC text):
   ```sql
   UPDATE public.profiles
   SET assigned_phc = 'PHC Rampur'
   WHERE id = 'REPLACE-WITH-ASHA-AUTH-USER-UUID';
   ```
6. For each existing PHC, make sure patient rows use the exact same PHC name:
   ```sql
   SELECT id, name, phc_name FROM public.maternal_patients;
   SELECT id, full_name, assigned_phc FROM public.profiles WHERE role = 'asha';
   ```
7. Add the following environment variables to Vercel (Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables), for Production and Preview as appropriate:
   - `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` = your Supabase Project URL
   - `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` = your Supabase anon/public key
   Use the same Supabase project values for every deployment/device. Never put a service-role key in frontend environment variables.
8. Redeploy the Vercel app after adding environment variables.

## Important notes
- A worker must be approved (`account_status = 'active'`) and assigned to the same PHC to see shared records.
- `profiles.assigned_phc` must exactly match `maternal_patients.phc_name`.
- Offline registrations and visits are queued in browser localStorage and are uploaded when the app is online and the user is logged in. Keep the same browser/device until the queue has synced; clearing browser storage before sync can lose queued records.
- This patch queues and syncs `REGISTER_MOTHER` and `RECORD_VISIT`. It intentionally does not mark unsupported queue item types as synced.
- Local-only demo accounts/data cannot be shared between devices. Shared operation requires Supabase credentials and Supabase Auth accounts on all devices.
- Existing localStorage-only patient records are not automatically migrated to Supabase by this change. Export/back up and import them separately before deleting local browser data.
- Test first with dummy records, never with real patient data until the PHC access rules have been reviewed by the project administrator.
